  "history_of_present_illness": "The patient is a 59\u2011year\u2011old Black male with a long\u2011standing history of type 2 diabetes\u2011related kidney disease progressing from CKD stage 1 in 2010 to CKD stage 3 by 2015, now awaiting kidney transplantation (since 2017). He has persistent proteinuria and microalbuminuria despite suboptimal renoprotective therapy. Cardiovascular disease is prominent, with ischemic heart disease diagnosed in 2011, atrial fibrillation since 2015, and essential hypertension since 2003, all treated with multiple agents. Metabolic syndrome, obesity (BMI\u202f\u2265\u202f30), and obstructive sleep apnea further compound his risk. He continues to smoke daily despite nicotine\u2011patch therapy. Recent medication list shows polypharmacy, including dual antithrombotic therapy (warfarin\u202f+\u202fclopidogrel) and an NSAID (naproxen) that are high\u2011risk in CKD. He reports ongoing knee osteoarthritis pain. The clinical trajectory is one of progressive renal decline, high cardiovascular risk, and preparation for transplant, with several modifiable risk factors inadequately addressed.",
